{"title":"Vehicle Network Engineer Roadmap","role":"Vehicle Network Engineer","summary":"A Vehicle Network Engineer designs, integrates, configures, tests, and troubleshoots the communication networks that allow electronic control units (ECUs), sensors, actuators, gateways, and vehicle computers to exchange information.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Automotive Electronics / Autonomous Vehicles"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Vehicle Network Engineer designs, integrates, configures, tests, and troubleshoots the communication networks that allow electronic control units (ECUs), sensors, actuators, gateways, and vehicle computers to exchange information."},{"type":"p","text":"Modern vehicles contain dozens of interconnected electronic systems. A Vehicle Network Engineer works at the intersection of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Automotive electronics"},{"text":"Embedded systems"},{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"CAN/LIN/FlexRay/Ethernet"},{"text":"Automotive diagnostics"},{"text":"AUTOSAR"},{"text":"Embedded software"},{"text":"Functional safety"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"ADAS and autonomous driving"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Designing ECU communication architectures"},{"text":"Configuring CAN/LIN/Ethernet networks"},{"text":"Analyzing communication traffic"},{"text":"Developing communication software"},{"text":"Diagnosing network faults"},{"text":"Implementing automotive diagnostics"},{"text":"Testing ECUs and vehicle networks"},{"text":"Working with gateways and domain controllers"},{"text":"Supporting ADAS/autonomous systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A realistic career path is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech","Automotive / Embedded Intern","Vehicle Network Engineer","Embedded / Automotive Network Engineer","Senior Vehicle Network Engin